  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Prevention, Detection, and Treatment of Diseases affecting US-bound Refugees and Other Globally Mobile Populations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM staff provide operational support and conduct health assessment activities through a global network of clinics and mobile health teams. These health assessment activities ensure that individuals from these populations are fit to travel, that they receive cost- effective interventions for select infectious diseases where indicated and available, and that communicable diseases of public health significance are identifies, managed, and reported.  The project will also implement research activities to examine alternative diagnostic and treatment regimens for select diseases, to develop and evaluate enhanced outbreak detection and response systems, and to investigate and characterize health conditions affecting globally mobile populations with the overall goal of strengthening health assessment procedures and disease prevention and control activities.</narrative>
  </description>
